{"item_uid": "指考93-english-011", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 93, "year_ce": 2004, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 20, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "", "options": {"A": "soon", "B": "also", "C": "thus", "D": "rather\n第 21 ㉃ 25 題為題組\nChildren’s encounters with poetry should include three types of response—enjoyment, exploration,\nand deepening understanding. These do not occur always as __21__ steps but may happen simultaneously.\nCertainly, children must start with enjoyment __22__ their interest in poetry dies. But if from the beginning\nthey find delight in the poems they hear or read, they are ready and eager to __23__ further—more books\nand more poems of different sorts. Even the youngest children can learn to see implications __24__ the\nobvious. To read for hidden meanings is to identify with the poet, to ask the poet’s questions. This is reading\nfor deeper understanding, __25__ a thoughtful look at what lies beneath the surface. Enjoyment, exploration,\nand deeper understanding must all be part of children’s experience with poetry if we are to help them to love\nit."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "C", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 17.0, "B": 13.0, "C": 40.0, "D": 13.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 2.0, "B": 94.0, "C": 2.0, "D": 1.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 13.0, "B": 45.0, "C": 16.0, "D": 17.0}, "omit_rate": 17.0, "p_value": 73.0, "p_high": 94.0, "p_low": 45.0, "discrimination": 49.0, "p_quintiles": [96.0, 89.0, 80.0, 63.0, 36.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
