{"item_uid": "指考93-english-026", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 93, "year_ce": 2004, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 50, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "According to the passage, which of the following statements is true about Robot Aibo?", "options": {"A": "It could recognize shapes and colors.", "B": "It could respond to spoken commands.", "C": "It was put on the market no later than 1990.", "D": "It was created much later than Cindy Smart."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "B", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 20.0, "B": 21.0, "C": 11.0, "D": 38.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 13.0, "B": 67.0, "C": 16.0, "D": 2.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 29.0, "B": 21.0, "C": 22.0, "D": 17.0, "E": 0.0}, "omit_rate": 10.0, "p_value": 42.0, "p_high": 67.0, "p_low": 21.0, "discrimination": 46.0, "p_quintiles": [76.0, 50.0, 36.0, 26.0, 19.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考93-english-027", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 93, "year_ce": 2004, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 51, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "The pronoun it in the fourth paragraph most likely refers to _____.", "options": {"A": "the process", "B": "the object", "C": "the radius", "D": "the request\n- 5 -\n93年指考 第 6 頁\n英文考科 共 7 頁"}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "D", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 14.0, "B": 45.0, "C": 9.0, "D": 22.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 9.0, "B": 14.0, "C": 5.0, "D": 68.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 24.0, "B": 30.0, "C": 17.0, "D": 14.0, "E": 0.0}, "omit_rate": 10.0, "p_value": 38.0, "p_high": 68.0, "p_low": 14.0, "discrimination": 54.0, "p_quintiles": [76.0, 52.0, 31.0, 18.0, 13.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考93-english-028", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 93, "year_ce": 2004, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 52, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "According to the passage, how can Cindy “see”?", "options": {"A": "She recognizes any text as “I love you.”", "B": "She is equipped with a camera to search for text.", "C": "She is instructed by an engineer standing next to her.", "D": "She makes contact with the shapes of the text with her belly.\n第 53㉃56題為題組\nIn June 1943, Frank Lloyd Wright received a letter from Hilla Rebay, the art adviser to Solomon R.\nGuggenheim, asking the architect to design a new building to house Guggenheim’s four-year-old museum of\nNon-Objective Painting. The project evolved into a complex struggle pitting the architect against his clients,\ncity officials, the art world, and public opinions. Both Guggenheim and Wright would die before the\nbuilding’s 1995 completion. The resultant achievement, the Solomon R. Guggenheim Museum, testifies not\nonly to Wright’s architectural genius, but also to the adventurous spirit that characterized its founders.\nWright made no secret of his disenchantment with Guggenheim’s choice of New York for his museum:\n“I can think of several more desirable places in the world to build this great museum,” Wright wrote in 1949\nto his partner, “but we will have to try New York.” To Wright, the city was overbuilt, overpopulated, and\nlacked architectural merit. Still, he proceeded with his client’s wishes, considering locations on 36th Street,\n54th Street, and Park Avenue (all in Manhattan), as well as in the Riverdale section of the Bronx, before\nsettling on the present site on Fifth Avenue between 88th and 89th Streets. Its nearness to Central Park was\nkey. As close to nature as one gets in New York, the park offered relief from the noise and congestion of the\ncity.\nWright’s design put his unique stamp on Modernist Architecture’s rigid geometry. The building is a\nsymphony of triangles, ovals, arcs, circles, and squares. The delicate vision took decades to be fulfilled.\nSome people, especially artists, criticized Wright for creating a museum environment that might overpower\nthe art inside. “On the contrary,” he wrote, “it was to make the building and the painting an uninterrupted,\nbeautiful symphony such as never existed in the world of art before.”\nIn conquering the regularity of geometric design and combining it with the plasticity of nature, Wright\nproduced a vibrant building whose architecture is as refreshing now as it was 40 years ago. The Guggenheim\nis arguably Wright’s most eloquent presentation and certainly the most important building of his late career."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "B", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 17.0, "B": 40.0, "C": 10.0, "D": 13.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 4.0, "B": 72.0, "C": 2.0, "D": 19.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 25.0, "B": 21.0, "C": 17.0, "D": 23.0, "E": 0.0}, "omit_rate": 19.0, "p_value": 45.0, "p_high": 72.0, "p_low": 21.0, "discrimination": 51.0, "p_quintiles": [77.0, 60.0, 42.0, 27.0, 18.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考93-english-029", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 93, "year_ce": 2004, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 53, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "The Guggenheim Museum was built __________.", "options": {"A": "in memory of Solomon Guggenheim", "B": "to keep Guggenheim’s art collections", "C": "for a famous symphony orchestra", "D": "at the request of New York city officials"}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "B", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 30.0, "B": 16.0, "C": 17.0, "D": 13.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 10.0, "B": 66.0, "C": 5.0, "D": 6.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 22.0, "B": 23.0, "C": 15.0, "D": 21.0, "E": 0.0}, "omit_rate": 24.0, "p_value": 40.0, "p_high": 66.0, "p_low": 23.0, "discrimination": 43.0, "p_quintiles": [77.0, 46.0, 32.0, 26.0, 21.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
{"item_uid": "指考93-english-030", "sitting": "regular", "exam_system": "指考", "year_roc": 93, "year_ce": 2004, "subject_key": "english", "subject_zh": "英文", "curriculum": "99課綱及以前", "number": 54, "join_excluded": false, "part": null, "stem": "According to the passage, why was Wright NOT enthusiastic about building the Guggenheim Museum\nin New York City?", "options": {"A": "There were already too many people and buildings in New York City.", "B": "There were not enough enthusiastic architects to design the museum.", "C": "There was very little support from residents in New York City.", "D": "There was strong objection from Solomon R. Guggenheim."}, "option_source": null, "group_id": null, "group_passage": null, "section": null, "keys": "A", "item_flags": [], "extracted_by": "pdf", "multi_select": false, "option_dist_T": {"A": 13.0, "B": 17.0, "C": 28.0, "D": 21.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_H": {"A": 52.0, "B": 8.0, "C": 12.0, "D": 13.0, "E": 0.0}, "option_dist_L": {"A": 15.0, "B": 24.0, "C": 23.0, "D": 13.0, "E": 0.0}, "omit_rate": 21.0, "p_value": 30.0, "p_high": 52.0, "p_low": 15.0, "discrimination": 37.0, "p_quintiles": [62.0, 35.0, 23.0, 17.0, 14.0], "hl_definition": "top_bottom_33pct"}
